  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bronsted base are those which can donate its lone pair to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> ion. The more easily the compound can donate its lone pair to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> strong will be a basic character.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d7bcdea9-744d-4ecc-ae5d-3a47efade98e.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 177px;\"/></p><p>Option D, is the strongest Bronsted base due to the availability of a lone pair which does not involve in any resonance.</p>",
